From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:02:05 +0200
Subject: nouveau, nv30: recover from a submission ps3rsx cancelled
 (PS3_RECOVER)

ps3rsx validates every push, because one bad command wedges the RSX until the console reboots.
Up to now a rejected push refused its channel for good (-EIO on every later submission): Mesa
sends state once and counts on it, so its next draws would have run on the GPU's older state.
The program then drew nothing for the rest of its life. ps3rsx now offers a recovery: a client
that asks for it (private GETPARAM 0x1001, PS3_RECOVER, before its channel exists) gets
-ECANCELED for a submission with a rejected push, none of which reached the GPU, and the
channel takes further submissions, each validated as always. This patch is that client.

Winsys: -ECANCELED counts in nouveau_device::cancelled (a line on stderr at the 1st, 2nd, 4th,
... cancellation, not the pushbuf dump). A push buffer whose cancel_seen lags behind it was
built on state that never reached the GPU (the rest of a draw the cancelled submission began,
a copy loop's lines after its DMA objects, state of other contexts on the channel): its kick
drops the queued words and submits only the fence kick_notify adds, so fences keep landing.

nv30: before a validation, a transfer or a buffer copy (not inside a validation), a context
whose push buffer lags runs nv30_state_lost(): the kick drops its queued words, and once per
cancellation the screen empties the vertex program and constant heaps (code and constants are
uploaded again where used, the blits' program too), bumps lost_gen (fragment programs and the
blit program are uploaded again) and forgets cur_ctx, so the next context to draw assumes
nothing of the GPU state and writes all of it (0029's path, also with NV30_CTX_STATE_KEEP).
What the cancelled submission uploaded or rendered is lost, as after a GPU reset. A program
that keeps sending something ps3rsx refuses draws nothing and keeps running.

Waits: a fence of the cancelled submission never lands; its waiter submits the context's
current fence and waits for that one. A query whose end may have been cancelled (a
cancellation since it was queued) and whose report isn't there is taken as lost: occlusion
"passed", times 0, instead of a wait that never ends.

NV30_PS3_RECOVER=0: not asked (the channel is refused as before). On an older ps3rsx the
GETPARAM fails and nothing changes. Not on the PS3 the counters never move.

Checked on the PC with ps3rsx's mesa-shim (the validator over every submit, ps3rsx's answers):
mpv --vo=gpu on this patch without 0052 has every frame cancelled for its X16 texture and keeps
playing, drawing nothing; with 0052 and one submit rejected by hand, the next frame re-sends the
whole state (346 words against 36) and the final GPU state equals the run without the rejection;
egl-gears, gl-mipread, gl-genmip and gl-texsub with 2-3 rejected submits each finish; what
reached the "GPU" passes the validator as one stream every time.

Forwarded: not-needed (ps3rsx only)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_fence.c
@@ -373,6 +373,19 @@ _nouveau_fence_wait(struct nouveau_fence *fence, struct util_debug_callback *deb
       }
 
       _nouveau_fence_update(screen, false);
+      /* ps3rsx cancelled the submission it was in (nouveau_device::cancelled): it never
+       * lands. The next fence to land after it signals it: submit the context's current one
+       * and wait for that (the kick drops what was queued on the lost state, not the fence). */
+      if (fence->state != NOUVEAU_FENCE_STATE_SIGNALLED && screen->device->cancelled &&
+          fence->context && fence->context->fence && fence->context->fence != fence) {
+         struct nouveau_fence *next = NULL;
+
+         _nouveau_fence_ref(fence->context->fence, &next);
+         if (nouveau_fence_kick(next) && next->bo)
+            nouveau_bo_wait(next->bo, NOUVEAU_BO_RDWR, screen->client);
+         _nouveau_fence_update(screen, false);
+         _nouveau_fence_ref(NULL, &next);
+      }
       if (fence->state != NOUVEAU_FENCE_STATE_SIGNALLED)
          return false;
 
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
@@ -335,6 +335,14 @@ nouveau_screen_init(struct nouveau_screen *screen, struct nouveau_device *dev)
                     vendor == 0x104d &&
                     !nouveau_getparam(dev, 0x1000 /* PS3_ABI */, &ps3_abi);
    screen->ps3_abi = screen->is_ps3 ? ps3_abi : 0;
+   /* ps3rsx's PS3_RECOVER, asked before the channel is made: a submission with a push its
+    * validator rejects is then cancelled (-ECANCELED, nouveau_device::cancelled) and the driver
+    * sends its state again (nv30_state_lost()), instead of the channel being refused for good.
+    * An older ps3rsx doesn't know it (the channel is refused, as before). NV30_PS3_RECOVER=0:
+    * not asked. */
+   uint64_t ps3_recover;
+   if (screen->is_ps3 && debug_get_bool_option("NV30_PS3_RECOVER", true))
+      nouveau_getparam(dev, 0x1001 /* PS3_RECOVER */, &ps3_recover);
    screen->ps3_relocs = screen->is_ps3 && debug_get_bool_option("NV30_PS3_RELOCS", false);
    if (screen->is_ps3) {
       nv04_data.vram = 0xfeed0000;
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_context.h
@@ -65,6 +65,13 @@ struct nv30_context {
    /* nv30_screen::tex_gen when this context last invalidated the texture cache */
    uint32_t tex_gen;
 
+   /* nv30_state_lost() ran: the next context switch assumes nothing of the GPU state, even
+    * with NV30_CTX_STATE_KEEP; in_validate: inside nv30_state_validate (no reset there);
+    * blit_fp_gen: nv30_screen::lost_gen when blit_fp was uploaded */
+   bool state_lost;
+   bool in_validate;
+   uint32_t blit_fp_gen;
+
    /* draws since the last submission of this context (NV30_PS3_KICK_DRAWS) */
    unsigned draws_since_kick;
 
@@ -247,6 +254,21 @@ nv30_render_vbo(struct pipe_context *pipe, const struct pipe_draw_info *info,
 bool
 nv30_state_validate(struct nv30_context *nv30, uint32_t mask, bool hwtnl);
 
+void
+nv30_state_lost(struct nv30_context *nv30);
+
+/* Before anything that sets GPU state or counts on it: after a cancelled submission
+ * (nouveau_device::cancelled moved past this context's push buffer), take nothing of the GPU
+ * state as known and send it all again (nv30_state_lost()). Not inside nv30_state_validate:
+ * the draw it validates for is dropped with the words already queued. */
+static inline void
+nv30_state_check_lost(struct nv30_context *nv30)
+{
+   if (unlikely(nv30->base.pushbuf->cancel_seen != nv30->screen->base.device->cancelled) &&
+       !nv30->in_validate)
+      nv30_state_lost(nv30);
+}
+
 void
 nv30_state_release(struct nv30_context *nv30);
 
